  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its scale and design, would result in a disproportionate addition to the property, almost doubling its width and overall footprint and&nbsp;projecting beyond the established building line along Campden Crescent, thus&nbsp;failing&nbsp;to appear subordinate to the host dwelling. The flat roofed design of the side and rear extensions would appear incongruous with the predominant roof forms in the area, creating a disjointed and visually poor appearance. Furthermore, the relocation of the main entrance would undermine a key architectural feature characteristic of the Becontree Estate. Taken together, the entrance relocation and the scale and form of the extensions would disrupt the established balance and symmetry that has been carefully preserved, harming the heritage significance of the dwelling and area.&nbsp;The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness:National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG) (December, 2024)Policies D4 and&nbsp;HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)&nbsp;"
  ],
